@flexiarg pattern-interpretation/put-uncertainty-in-theta
@title Put Uncertainty In q0 Or θ, Preference In C, And Keep Unknown For Unobserved
@keywords theta, prior, outcome, want, coverage, observation, preference
@audience interpretation jobs, cascade-model builders
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-16 (claude-7; findings F2, F3; claude-4 agreed to make attested θ required (D6) and to score want coverage on predicted observation (D7))
@references [pattern-interpretation/declare-the-universe pattern-interpretation/compile-guards-exactly translation/declare-what-is-lost]
@see-also buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness
@how split by what the uncertainty is about: uncertainty about the current state goes in q0 as a distribution over states; uncertainty about what an act achieves goes in the attested θ of the acting pattern; how much an outcome is wanted goes in C, which holds preference only. None of these becomes a guard over an :unknown fact. "Needed later" is about the future, so it is θ (or q0 if it is a present, unobserved fact), never C. θ is one number per pattern for its whole effect set (P3), so an act with a near-certain direct token (the edit is made) and an uncertain outcome token (the repo is clean) is split into linked parts (:source-pattern, :part), one token per part with its own θ; per-token θ within one pattern is not in the approved design. A want that is a world outcome is added as a θ-weighted effect of the pattern whose act brings it about, and coverage is scored on the predicted observation of that token, so a fix that is confirmed only by the next tick's observation is counted as predicted, not as done.
@violation-signature a guard NOT needed-later that can never fire; a world prior placed in C; one θ covering a certain direct effect and an uncertain outcome; θ left at the documented default 1 for an outcome with a declared prior; want coverage computed over produced tokens at θ = 1.
! conclusion: Present-state uncertainty lives in q0, uncertainty about what an act achieves in θ (split into parts when effects differ in certainty), preference in C, outcome wants are θ-weighted effects scored on predicted observation, and unknown is kept for unobserved facts.

  + context: Flexiargs such as buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness state priors (temp 0.05, dired 0.25, file-stale 0.40 at 6 h).

  + IF:
    A pattern's prose expresses uncertainty about outcomes or names a goal state.

  + HOWEVER:
    The guard language is logical and the effect language is add-only and certain.

  + THEN:
    Put present-state uncertainty in q0 and act uncertainty in θ, keep C for preference, split acts whose effects differ in certainty, and give outcome wants a θ-weighted producing part scored by observation.

  + BECAUSE:
    Guards decide whether an act may happen; q0 says what is believed now, θ what the act is expected to achieve, and C how much that is wanted.

  + evidence: worked instances §1 (clean-enough never produced), §2 (repo-clean likewise); claude-4's tick-1 observation that "partial summary observes cleanly" is established by the fix but confirmed only at the next tick.
